# PRIORITY 1 — FIX FIRESTORE AS SOURCE OF TRUTH

## Known defect

The existing persistence manager loads local data before cloud synchronization and may merge Firestore data into an existing local map.

It may also seed an empty Firestore collection with local records automatically.

This can preserve stale records or promote outdated local data into the authoritative cloud database.

## Required implementation

Define an explicit persistence policy.

### Production

1. Firestore must be the authoritative source for cloud curriculum records.
2. A local cache must never silently override newer cloud data.
3. An empty Firestore collection must not trigger an unrestricted local-data import.
4. Any initial import must be an explicit, authorized, auditable migration.
5. Define deterministic conflict-resolution rules.
6. Distinguish cached data from confirmed cloud data.
7. If cloud synchronization fails, do not present stale local records as confirmed current production data.
8. Prevent duplicate source records during retries.
9. Include grade and source boundaries in all reconciliation logic.
10. Preserve data needed for safe recovery.

### Development

Local development support may remain, but development persistence must be separated explicitly from production persistence.

### Acceptance tests

Test:

- Empty Firestore.
- Non-empty Firestore.
- Stale local records.
- Newer cloud records.
- Conflicting local and cloud versions.
- Firestore timeout.
- Recovery after timeout.
- Explicit initial migration.
- Repeated synchronization.
- Separate grade datasets.

